WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
Northern Ireland, 21
March 2021: census day.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:14.870
The count found 1,903,175
people, in 768,810 households.

3
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.250
In Kenya, the 2019 census was the
country's first paperless one,

4
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.410
run on mobile devices.

5
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.290
But some people slip through any count.

6
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.970
So how do you count every
person in a country,

7
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.150
and how do you know who was missed?

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.070
In this mission, you'll picture
a population as water in a bath,

9
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.250
and work out how to measure it.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.750
Then you'll compare
Northern Ireland with Kenya,

11
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.210
and test how reliable each
country's numbers are.

12
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.610
Your mission: find out how
a country counts its people,

13
00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.600
and how it spots who was missed.
